# Build-context ignore file for `docker build`/`docker compose build` invocations that use
# mu-core/ as their context (e.g. packages/mu-engine-server/Dockerfile — see that file's own
# header comment for why its context is the workspace root, not its own directory).
#
# ADDED BY: Stage E (mu-engine-server docker/compose/Makefile build agent, build-plan §4 Stage E,
# E1). NOTE ON SCOPE: this task's file ownership is scoped to packages/mu-engine-server/*; this
# root-level file is the one necessary exception, added only because it is load-bearing for
# correctness/practicality, not style. Rationale, verified empirically in this environment:
# `packages/mu-engine-server/Dockerfile.dockerignore` (the per-Dockerfile ignore-file convention,
# which WOULD have kept this entirely inside that package's own directory) is a BuildKit-only
# feature — this host's Docker CLI has no `buildx` plugin installed (`docker buildx version` ->
# "unknown command"), so `docker build`/`docker compose build` here fall back to the classic
# builder, which only ever reads a `.dockerignore` at the CONTEXT ROOT. Without this file, every
# build tars/streams this entire directory to the daemon verbatim — observed directly: `docker
# compose up -d --build` never even reached container creation after 5+ minutes with this file
# absent, because `.venv` alone is 5.4G of mostly-tiny site-packages files (`du -sh
# mu-core/.venv` = 5.4G, `.mypy_cache` = 170M) that classic `docker build` has no other way to
# skip. None of the excluded paths below are referenced by any `COPY` in that Dockerfile.

# Local dev virtualenv / caches — never needed in the image; the Dockerfile's own builder stage
# creates a fresh `.venv` via `uv sync --no-editable`.
.venv
**/.venv
.mypy_cache
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.import_linter_cache
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info

# VCS / editor / misc repo furniture not needed to build or run the image
.git
.gitignore
.trash
logs
graphify-out
.claude

# Test trees — exercised by CI against source directly, not needed inside the built image
packages/*/tests
